    "body": "`BerkeleyRODatabase::Open` reads an overflow record by following `next_page` until it is 0. #34959 added a check that stops once more data than `item_len` was read, which needs every page to add data. An overflow page with `hf_offset` 0 adds none. If such a page names itself as `next_page`, the loop reads it again and again and never ends.\n\nThis PR treats an overflow page without data as corruption.\n\n**Behavior change:** a file with an empty overflow page no longer opens and fails with `Overflow page has no data`. Before, an empty page with `next_page` 0 was accepted and the record came out shorter than `item_len`.\n\n**Measurement:** regtest, RelWithDebInfo, base a527a0077a. The file has 5 pages of 4096 bytes: one key whose value is an overflow record with `item_len` 100, and one overflow page.\n\n| overflow page | master | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `hf_offset` 0, `next_page` itself | `bitcoin-wallet dump` at 100 % of one core, killed after 60 s | fails at once, exit 1 |\n| `hf_offset` 100, `next_page` 0 | dumped in 0.11 s | dumped as before |\n\nWith `migratewallet` on master the RPC does not return and one HTTP worker stays at 100 % CPU. Other RPCs still answer, but `stop` had not finished after 30 s.\n\n**Tests:** new case in `tool_wallet.py` that writes both files by hand. On master it hangs (killed after 90 s). Passing locally: `test_bitcoin` and `test_runner.py` with the default list. Not run: fuzz targets, lint.\n\nContributed by [turingpoint](https://www.turingpoint.de).\n",
