          "sha": "a527a0077a0fcae913188410214efe98021c0cca",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/a527a0077a0fcae913188410214efe98021c0cca"
        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet, bdbro: Reject overflow pages without data\n\nAn overflow record is read by following next_page until it is 0. The\nlength check added in dc3a2b9c3b6 stops the loop once more data than\nitem_len was read, which needs every page to add data. An overflow\npage with hf_offset 0 adds nothing, so a page like that which names\nitself as next_page is read again and again. bitcoin-wallet dump and\nmigratewallet then spin on one core and never return.\n\nBDB does not write overflow pages without data, so treat one as\ncorruption.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jan Kahmen <jan@turingpoint.de>",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Jan Kahmen",
        "email": "36455663+kah-ja@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-16T05:54:35Z"
